{"id":"leetcode-17","version":1,"status":"approved","title":"Letter Combinations of a Phone Number","summary":"Given a string of digits from 2 to 9, generate all possible letter combinations corresponding to the digits.","statement":"Given a string of digits from 2 to 9, generate all possible letter combinations corresponding to the digits. Return the results in any order. Note that digit 1 does not map to any letters.","constraints":["1–4 digits, each from 2 through 9.","Mappings: 2→abc, 3→def, 4→ghi, 5→jkl, 6→mno, 7→pqrs, 8→tuv, 9→wxyz.","Return every combination exactly once, in any order."],"topics":["strings","recursion","backtracking"],"prerequisites":[],"signature":{"name":"phone_combinations","parameters":[{"name":"digits","annotation":"str","adapter":"raw","source_parameter":null}],"returns":"list[str]","return_adapter":"raw","node_policy":"values","result_mode":"return","mutated_parameter":null,"immutable_parameters":[]},"starter_code":"def phone_combinations(digits: str) -> list[str]:\n    # Write your solution here.\n    pass\n","reference_solution":"def phone_combinations(digits):\n    mapping = {\"2\":\"abc\", \"3\":\"def\", \"4\":\"ghi\", \"5\":\"jkl\", \"6\":\"mno\", \"7\":\"pqrs\", \"8\":\"tuv\", \"9\":\"wxyz\"}\n    answer, path = [], []\n    def visit(index):\n        if index == len(digits):\n            answer.append(\"\".join(path))\n            return\n        for letter in mapping[digits[index]]:\n            path.append(letter)\n            visit(index + 1)\n            path.pop()\n    visit(0)\n    return answer\n","brute_force_solution":null,"known_wrong_solutions":["def phone_combinations(digits):\n    mapping = {\"2\":\"abc\", \"3\":\"def\", \"4\":\"ghi\", \"5\":\"jkl\", \"6\":\"mno\", \"7\":\"pqr\", \"8\":\"tuv\", \"9\":\"wxy\"}\n    answer, path = [], []\n    def visit(index):\n        if index == len(digits):\n            answer.append(\"\".join(path))\n            return\n        for letter in mapping[digits[index]]:\n            path.append(letter)\n            visit(index + 1)\n            path.pop()\n    visit(0)\n    return answer\n","def phone_combinations(digits):\n    mapping = {\"2\":\"abc\", \"3\":\"def\", \"4\":\"ghi\", \"5\":\"jkl\", \"6\":\"mno\", \"7\":\"pqrs\", \"8\":\"tuv\", \"9\":\"wxyz\"}\n    answer, path = [], []\n    def visit(index):\n        if index == len(digits):\n            answer.append(\"\".join(path))\n            return\n        for letter in mapping[digits[index]][:1]:\n            path.append(letter)\n            visit(index + 1)\n            path.pop()\n    visit(0)\n    return answer\n"],"target_time_complexity":"O(d × 4^d)","target_space_complexity":"O(d) excluding output","estimated_minutes":35,"rubric":{"algorithmic_insight":2,"prerequisites":1,"implementation":1,"performance_pressure":1,"edge_cases":0},"hints":["Each output chooses exactly one letter per input position.","Track a prefix and branch over the current digit's letters.","At the end save the joined prefix; otherwise append a letter, recurse to the next position, then undo the append.","Digits 7 and 9 have four branches, not three."],"editorial":"The recursion depth identifies the next digit and the path stores letters already chosen. Explore each mapped letter, recurse, then remove it so sibling branches share only the unchanged prefix. Each leaf is a distinct choice vector and produces one output string. The maximum branching factor is four; output construction takes O(d·4^d) time and O(d) auxiliary stack space excluding results.","tests":[{"id":"lc-17-1","arguments":["23"],"expected":["ad","ae","af","bd","be","bf","cd","ce","cf"],"comparator":"unordered","visible":true,"explanation":"Choose one of a/b/c followed by one of d/e/f: three times three gives nine strings.","expected_node_order":null},{"id":"lc-17-2","arguments":["7"],"expected":["p","q","r","s"],"comparator":"unordered","visible":true,"explanation":"Digit 7 has four letters, so return p, q, r, and s as separate one-letter strings.",